1
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:04,210
"Instead"?!

2
00:00:04,210 --> 00:00:04,900
Yes.

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,520
Where's the old hag?

4
00:00:06,770 --> 00:00:08,610
I couldn't foresee what would happen,

5
00:00:08,610 --> 00:00:10,030
so I had her go elsewhere.

6
00:00:10,290 --> 00:00:13,530
And what the hell are you still doin' here?

7
00:00:13,530 --> 00:00:16,160
You wanna "talk things over," but the 
one you wanna talk to ain't even here!

8
00:00:16,390 --> 00:00:17,680
That's true.

9
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:23,290
So I guess we'll just say I'm buying time so a 
certain boy and girl can be alone for a while.

10
00:00:24,490 --> 00:00:26,000
Oh, really?!

11
00:00:29,250 --> 00:00:32,380
You ain't got what it takes, small fry.

12
00:00:37,540 --> 00:00:38,350
The stone—

13
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:44,920
Damn it...

14
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:48,460
Is this what you're looking for?

15
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:54,160
A merchant always keeps one step ahead 
to ascertain his chances of success,

16
00:00:54,580 --> 00:00:55,820
and that's what I am.

17
00:00:56,120 --> 00:00:57,490
You piece of...

18
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:03,120
I've never had very many human friends,

19
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:05,950
but I made lots of non-human 
friends instead.

20
00:01:07,090 --> 00:01:09,320
The entire forest is against you now.

21
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:12,810
Enjoy this welcome from 
the zodda bugs first!

22
00:01:15,690 --> 00:01:17,900
Damn it... Damn it!

23
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:20,010
Damn it!

24
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:34,110
<i>When I was a young boy,</i>

25
00:01:34,110 --> 00:01:36,280
<i>the world was a hellish cradle.</i>

26
00:01:39,620 --> 00:01:42,820
<i>No matter where I went, 
I heard endless voices,</i>

27
00:01:42,820 --> 00:01:45,750
<i>but had no idea what any 
of them were saying.</i>

28
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:51,530
<i>At that age, I had no way to know that 
this was the blessing I was born with,</i>

29
00:01:51,530 --> 00:01:54,220
<i>the "soul of language" divine protection.</i>

30
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:56,610
Wait up!

31
00:02:00,270 --> 00:02:02,140
Otto, what are you doing?

32
00:02:04,850 --> 00:02:06,430
You're not going to play with them?

33
00:02:08,530 --> 00:02:12,940
<i>My parents tried their hardest 
to understand my abnormality,</i>

34
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:18,200
<i>but any who don't have a divine 
protection can never understand.</i>

35
00:02:35,140 --> 00:02:37,080
Otto, try writing it.

36
00:02:43,860 --> 00:02:46,730
<i>It was my brother, seven years my senior,</i>

37
00:02:46,730 --> 00:02:50,360
<i>who realized that written words might 
bring about that understanding</i>

38
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:52,170
<i>when spoken words couldn't.</i>

39
00:03:16,090 --> 00:03:17,420
Otto...

40
00:03:29,620 --> 00:03:33,820
<i>That may have been the first time 
I'd cried out since I was born.</i>

41
00:03:38,290 --> 00:03:40,770
<i>Then when I turned ten...</i>

42
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:57,380
Big... light... went... that way...

43
00:03:57,700 --> 00:04:02,170
<i>Those meaningless voices started to 
transform into sounds with meaning.</i>

44
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:04,640
You can understand what animals say?

45
00:04:04,990 --> 00:04:05,740
Yeah.

46
00:04:08,130 --> 00:04:10,810
Rain... fall soon. Rain soon.

47
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:13,010
They say it's going to rain soon.

48
00:04:13,010 --> 00:04:13,660
Huh?

49
00:04:22,290 --> 00:04:24,910
Otto, that's an amazing power.

50
00:04:25,230 --> 00:04:26,570
And because it's so amazing,

51
00:04:26,570 --> 00:04:30,320
you shouldn't talk to zodda 
bugs when people are around.

52
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:31,120
Why not?

53
00:04:31,580 --> 00:04:34,100
Divine protections are blessings 
granted by this world,

54
00:04:34,100 --> 00:04:36,580
but there are people who would 
try to take advantage of it.

55
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:38,920
You have to keep your power hidden.

56
00:04:40,410 --> 00:04:44,590
That's why I can't talk to you around 
other people anymore, Fulfew.

57
00:04:45,020 --> 00:04:47,280
I understand, Young Master.

58
00:04:47,930 --> 00:04:49,070
Liar!

59
00:04:49,070 --> 00:04:50,790
Liar! Liar!

60
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:51,760
You're just a liar!

61
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:52,790
We know it's all lies!

62
00:04:52,790 --> 00:04:53,620
You're so lying!

63
00:04:53,620 --> 00:04:55,270
I'm not lying!

64
00:04:55,270 --> 00:04:58,510
My big brother Otto can talk to animals!

65
00:04:59,550 --> 00:05:01,440
Can't you, Otto?!

66
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:21,370
It's true!

67
00:05:21,370 --> 00:05:22,170
Zodda bugs!

68
00:05:26,340 --> 00:05:28,930
Oh, no! Zodda bugs!

69
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:35,230
You zodda bug freak!

70
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:41,270
<i>After that, I sealed my divine protection</i>

71
00:05:41,270 --> 00:05:43,710
<i>and swore never to use it again.</i>

72
00:05:46,410 --> 00:05:48,530
<i>Then when I was fifteen...</i>

73
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:54,160
You son of a bitch! I know 
you were with my girlfriend!

74
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:56,510
W-Wait a—

75
00:05:55,450 --> 00:05:57,920
Shut the hell up, you zodda bug freak!

76
00:05:58,130 --> 00:06:01,170
Zodda bug... freak?

77
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:05,260
I'm gonna find out the truth!

78
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:06,880
I saw.

79
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:34,830
I know the truth!

80
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:37,830
You're the eighth guy she's been with!

81
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:39,750
You jerk!

82
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:43,090
Someone kill him!

83
00:06:47,370 --> 00:06:50,550
<i>I made an enemy of the daughter of 
the most powerful person in town,</i>

84
00:06:50,550 --> 00:06:52,670
<i>and they ran me out.</i>

85
00:06:58,540 --> 00:07:02,760
<i>After that, I unexpectedly found 
my independence as a merchant,</i>

86
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:04,520
<i>and I busted my butt working.</i>

87
00:07:08,660 --> 00:07:13,410
<i>I made up my mind that I'd 
run my own shop one day.</i>

88
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:19,990
<i>You can do it, Otto!</i>

89
00:07:20,770 --> 00:07:22,700
<i>Go, go, Otto!</i>

90
00:07:29,690 --> 00:07:31,770
Well, well, well...

91
00:07:31,770 --> 00:07:34,470
Where are you off to in such a...

92
00:07:34,880 --> 00:07:35,970
hurry?!

93
00:08:12,630 --> 00:08:14,800
You're one lucky boy.

94
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:17,510
You woulda been killed if I hadn't found ya.

95
00:08:17,890 --> 00:08:20,980
Better be grateful to the boss kid.

96
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:23,410
B-Boss... kid?

97
00:08:23,410 --> 00:08:24,770
Yeah, he's our boss.

98
00:08:24,980 --> 00:08:28,140
And he's the guy who saved your life.

99
00:08:28,140 --> 00:08:31,520
I-I understand. Thank you very much.

100
00:08:31,990 --> 00:08:33,530
And I should thank him, too.

101
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:37,120
If yer gonna cry, go hide first.

102
00:08:38,170 --> 00:08:41,210
No man should start sobbin' 
in front of anyone.

103
00:08:41,210 --> 00:08:43,520
Huh? C-Cry?

104
00:08:49,010 --> 00:08:49,880
Darn it...

105
00:08:51,620 --> 00:08:52,690
What is this?

106
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:56,570
This... Th-This...

107
00:08:59,850 --> 00:09:04,500
I... I'm so glad I didn't die...

108
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:09,920
<i>I realized that every time I cry, 
it marks a rebirth in my life.</i>

109
00:09:10,470 --> 00:09:13,440
<i>My first cry as a baby 
after receiving life...</i>

110
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:15,650
<i>My second cry after learning</i>

111
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:19,580
<i>of my family's love and realizing 
where my heart lay...</i>

112
00:09:20,030 --> 00:09:23,240
<i>And this day, the third, 
when I had a brush with death,</i>

113
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:27,240
<i>and gained an understanding of my 
purpose and reason for living.</i>

114
00:09:29,170 --> 00:09:33,670
I wasn't actually asked 
to buy time this way...

115
00:09:33,670 --> 00:09:36,190
But it's all to help my friend!

116
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:44,600
...coming! Coming!

117
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:45,920
Bad one coming!

118
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:47,060
I know that!

119
00:09:47,340 --> 00:09:49,520
Right behind you. Already here.

120
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:51,450
I said I <i>know</i> that!

121
00:09:51,450 --> 00:09:53,980
I planned for it! It's all 
part of the calculation!

122
00:09:53,980 --> 00:09:56,240
You're going to die. Poor thing.

123
00:09:56,450 --> 00:10:00,220
Could you please stop being so pessimistic?!

124
00:10:08,020 --> 00:10:11,150
Is this what happens when I keep using it?

125
00:10:11,150 --> 00:10:14,420
My divine protection is such a hassle.

126
00:10:15,250 --> 00:10:20,140
I wonder if Natsuki-san... is getting 
his chance to talk to Emilia-sama.

127
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:46,040
Found ya!

128
00:10:57,390 --> 00:10:58,700
Damn you!

129
00:10:59,510 --> 00:11:02,680
I was given a really exciting 
role to play for once!

130
00:11:02,680 --> 00:11:05,180
I'm not letting you catch me that easily!

131
00:11:33,220 --> 00:11:35,540
Come on, give me a break...

132
00:11:35,540 --> 00:11:37,210
I don't think so!

133
00:11:42,390 --> 00:11:45,390
I'm not lettin' you pull 
any of your shit again!

134
00:11:45,770 --> 00:11:48,210
I... I wouldn't be so sure...

135
00:11:48,570 --> 00:11:50,570
This fight isn't over ye—

136
00:11:51,330 --> 00:11:54,020
I told you, I'm not lettin' 
you pull any shit!

137
00:11:54,530 --> 00:11:56,720
Frankly, you surprised me.

138
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:59,980
I seriously never woulda 
thought you had it in ya.

139
00:12:01,510 --> 00:12:05,790
You'll hafta forgive me for doin' 
somethin' so shitty to a man.

140
00:12:08,410 --> 00:12:11,460
I think I've done all I could.

141
00:12:11,660 --> 00:12:13,850
Gimme the stone back right now!

142
00:12:13,850 --> 00:12:15,290
Enough already, damn it!

143
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:22,920
A'right, then. When you 
wake up, this'll all be—

144
00:12:22,920 --> 00:12:26,680
Let's just say my personal battle ends here.

145
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:29,180
Ram!

146
00:12:29,180 --> 00:12:30,060
El Fula!

147
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:32,400
Cocky bitch!

148
00:12:36,570 --> 00:12:40,090
Not that I didn't know it, but you're 
so pathetic, I couldn't watch.

149
00:12:40,090 --> 00:12:44,360
Isn't that a little harsh toward someone 
who just gave all he had fighting?

150
00:12:44,570 --> 00:12:47,120
All you had? In the state you're in?

151
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:51,140
I've never seen a maid as well-described 
as the polar opposite of soothing!

152
00:12:51,140 --> 00:12:53,410
Hey, Ram, doesn't joining their side mean

153
00:12:53,410 --> 00:12:57,130
you're goin' against what 
that bastard Roswaal wants?

154
00:12:57,530 --> 00:13:00,400
I would give my very soul to fulfill 
my master's fondest desire.

155
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:01,590
But...

156
00:13:02,020 --> 00:13:03,800
in my own way.

157
00:13:04,040 --> 00:13:05,830
Cut the shit!

158
00:13:05,830 --> 00:13:09,850
What do you think is happenin' 
while you keep me here?!

159
00:13:09,850 --> 00:13:13,220
You really think he's worth 
trustin' that much?!

160
00:13:13,220 --> 00:13:15,170
Is Natsuki-san worth it?

161
00:13:15,550 --> 00:13:18,480
Well, if we're talking about 
whether he's worth anything,

162
00:13:18,480 --> 00:13:19,960
I suppose he's not.

163
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:20,800
Huh?!

164
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:23,840
But I look forward to seeing 
what flowers bloom from him,

165
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:26,080
so I keep pruning and 
brushing off the bugs...

166
00:13:27,760 --> 00:13:29,910
I suppose that's the mood I'm in now.

167
00:13:30,160 --> 00:13:35,900
Hmph. Frankly, I have no idea what 
gives you such high hopes for Barusu.

168
00:13:36,820 --> 00:13:41,380
He's weak, useless, and so incompetent, 
he can't even make tea right.

169
00:13:41,380 --> 00:13:45,130
That's going a bit too far... 
or maybe not, actually.

170
00:13:45,440 --> 00:13:48,690
But... when it's do or die,

171
00:13:48,690 --> 00:13:50,470
he has bizarrely good timing.

172
00:13:52,430 --> 00:13:54,040
A man who only has good timing.

173
00:13:54,040 --> 00:13:55,230
That's what Barusu is.

174
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:59,890
If he believes he sees an 
opportunity and acts on it,

175
00:14:00,540 --> 00:14:02,820
you know that's the only path to victory.

176
00:14:03,070 --> 00:14:06,760
I guess when all's said and done, 
you trust Natsuki-san too, Ram-san.

177
00:14:06,760 --> 00:14:07,790
That's "Ram-sama."

178
00:14:07,790 --> 00:14:09,950
That's such a hostile way 
to hide your shyness!

179
00:14:11,620 --> 00:14:13,490
Enough!

180
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:26,540
Stay back.

181
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:27,970
Wait... Ram-san!

182
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:41,390
Have you ever once beaten me in a punch-out?

183
00:14:47,330 --> 00:14:48,900
No... way...

184
00:15:01,840 --> 00:15:04,130
You've gotten stronger, Garf.

185
00:15:24,080 --> 00:15:25,900
Al Fula!

186
00:15:32,130 --> 00:15:35,950
I'm counting on you, Otto. 
Please don't do anything crazy.

187
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:38,700
Now...

188
00:15:39,860 --> 00:15:41,960
I'm going to do my part.

189
00:15:46,610 --> 00:15:49,320
Oh, good. I finally found you.

190
00:15:53,930 --> 00:15:56,930
Otto Suwen

191
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:03,940
You really thought this through, 
didn't you, Emilia-tan?

192
00:16:04,190 --> 00:16:07,340
You knew no one would find 
you if you holed up in here.

193
00:16:08,270 --> 00:16:13,010
Why... are you here, Subaru? You don't...

194
00:16:13,010 --> 00:16:16,060
...get forced back as hard as Roswaal?

195
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:21,450
I mean, I'm here, but I'm
fighting pretty hard to endure.

196
00:16:21,830 --> 00:16:23,760
I... see...

197
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:28,780
Half of me believed you'd be here, 
and half of me just wished for it.

198
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:31,650
Half... and half...

199
00:16:31,650 --> 00:16:33,660
I'm so relieved that I found you.

200
00:16:34,540 --> 00:16:36,400
Just... relieved?

201
00:16:37,270 --> 00:16:39,330
You're not angry?

202
00:16:39,330 --> 00:16:41,410
What's this about, Emilia-tan?

203
00:16:41,410 --> 00:16:44,470
Were you actually afraid I'd be mad at you?

204
00:16:44,470 --> 00:16:46,220
I'm not angry.

205
00:16:46,220 --> 00:16:49,400
Though I did panic, and frankly, 
I wasn't even sure I was alive.

206
00:16:49,940 --> 00:16:52,640
I see. You're not angry.

207
00:16:52,990 --> 00:16:53,870
Emilia?

208
00:16:56,050 --> 00:16:59,550
You're not angry at me, Subaru.

209
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:03,020
You won't even get angry.

210
00:17:04,420 --> 00:17:07,660
Why won't you get angry?

211
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:11,280
What I did was selfish, wasn't it?

212
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:13,010
It caused trouble for you, didn't it?

213
00:17:13,370 --> 00:17:16,400
I worried you by leaving 
without saying anything.

214
00:17:17,220 --> 00:17:21,090
Are you not angry because you d-didn't 
expect anything in the first place?

215
00:17:21,090 --> 00:17:24,880
You're kind to me even when I mess up

216
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:27,060
because you're not even 
disappointed in me, right?

217
00:17:27,060 --> 00:17:30,690
Because you know it's 
never going to go right?

218
00:17:30,930 --> 00:17:33,870
No, Emilia! That's not what I think!

219
00:17:33,870 --> 00:17:35,070
Then...

220
00:17:35,900 --> 00:17:37,450
Then why?

221
00:17:38,420 --> 00:17:41,300
Why didn't you keep your promise?!

222
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:45,660
You and Puck both broke 
your word and went away.

223
00:17:46,140 --> 00:17:49,220
You went away and left me behind.

224
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:51,950
You're a liar.

225
00:17:52,520 --> 00:17:54,080
Puck is a liar.

226
00:17:55,670 --> 00:17:56,700
Liar...

227
00:17:57,780 --> 00:17:59,090
You liar...

228
00:17:59,090 --> 00:17:59,900
Emilia...

229
00:17:59,900 --> 00:18:02,760
You shouldn't... break a promise...

230
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:04,720
You shouldn't lie!

231
00:18:05,010 --> 00:18:06,720
It's wrong!

232
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:21,710
Emilia...

233
00:18:22,570 --> 00:18:24,620
I love you.

234
00:18:24,990 --> 00:18:25,580
Huh?

235
00:18:28,120 --> 00:18:32,460
Night after night, you go rushing into 
the same damn trial over and over.

236
00:18:32,460 --> 00:18:35,630
What the hell is that trial, anyway?
 It's just the past!

237
00:18:35,630 --> 00:18:38,530
Don't keep moping over stuff 
that's over and done with!

238
00:18:38,530 --> 00:18:39,680
Uh, wha...

239
00:18:39,680 --> 00:18:44,400
When I tried to do it for you, you 
insisted that only you could do it.

240
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:47,070
So when you blow it, that just 
means you were all talk!

241
00:18:47,070 --> 00:18:48,570
S-Subaru...

242
00:18:48,570 --> 00:18:51,610
And in the end, when your 
pet and guardian takes off,

243
00:18:51,610 --> 00:18:54,570
you abandon your duties and run off 
to sulk and cry your eyes out?

244
00:18:54,570 --> 00:18:56,530
I can't put up with it any longer!

245
00:19:00,420 --> 00:19:02,210
You're right.

246
00:19:02,210 --> 00:19:06,490
It only makes sense that 
you'd think of me that way.

247
00:19:06,700 --> 00:19:07,450
But still...

248
00:19:08,540 --> 00:19:11,920
I love you, Emilia.

249
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:16,660
I love you.

250
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:21,590
I love you so, so, so much, I don't 
know what to do with myself.

251
00:19:21,900 --> 00:19:24,340
Wh-Where did all this come from?

252
00:19:24,340 --> 00:19:27,360
I love that beautiful silver hair of yours,

253
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:30,640
I love those damp purple 
jewels you have for eyes.

254
00:19:31,040 --> 00:19:34,230
I love your voice and how just 
hearing it puts me in a trance.

255
00:19:34,430 --> 00:19:37,870
Your long, slender arms 
and legs, your pale skin,

256
00:19:38,240 --> 00:19:41,820
and your height are all so perfect 
to me that I can't stand it.

257
00:19:41,820 --> 00:19:44,450
Just being with you makes my 
heart race out of control.

258
00:19:44,450 --> 00:19:45,370
It's scary, honestly.

259
00:19:47,330 --> 00:19:49,700
I love how you're a little 
absent-minded, too.

260
00:19:49,700 --> 00:19:52,300
The way you give everything 
your all is adorable,

261
00:19:52,690 --> 00:19:55,870
and I respect the way you do 
your best to help others.

262
00:19:56,260 --> 00:19:59,960
It's hard to leave you alone when I see 
you putting others before yourself.

263
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:04,530
I want to see all the expressions you 
make from right here beside you.

264
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:07,740
Th-This is no time for...

265
00:20:08,470 --> 00:20:10,450
Stop playing around!

266
00:20:10,450 --> 00:20:13,040
Why are you suddenly saying all this?!

267
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:15,300
That's not what we were talking about!

268
00:20:15,300 --> 00:20:17,810
You were saying that I'm utterly useless,

269
00:20:17,810 --> 00:20:19,110
that you couldn't put up with me!

270
00:20:19,110 --> 00:20:20,400
Yeah, you're right.

271
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:23,460
So why would you forgive 
me for being so useless?!

272
00:20:23,460 --> 00:20:26,450
If that answer is all you want, 
I've said it over and over!

273
00:20:26,780 --> 00:20:29,450
It's because I love you!

274
00:20:31,250 --> 00:20:33,390
I'm head-over-heels in love with you!

275
00:20:33,390 --> 00:20:36,240
Everything about you shines in my eyes!

276
00:20:36,710 --> 00:20:39,060
Yeah, of course, parts of you aren't perfect.

277
00:20:39,060 --> 00:20:42,210
You're not an angel or a goddess. 
You're an ordinary girl.

278
00:20:42,210 --> 00:20:44,770
You'll feel so bad that you 
want to cry sometimes,

279
00:20:44,770 --> 00:20:48,220
and you'll want to run away from 
things that hurt! I get that!

280
00:20:48,510 --> 00:20:53,630
But even including that weakness and 
the parts you might even call ugly...

281
00:20:54,290 --> 00:20:57,110
I love every part of your being, Emilia.

282
00:20:58,460 --> 00:21:01,760
That's just... t-too selfish!

283
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:04,120
You just named all the things 
that make me useless,

284
00:21:04,690 --> 00:21:06,700
and you still say you love me?

285
00:21:07,430 --> 00:21:08,990
How can you expect me to believe you?!

286
00:21:08,990 --> 00:21:12,130
You're wrong! You've got 
it completely wrong!

287
00:21:12,130 --> 00:21:16,510
It's not because I believe 
in you that I love you!

288
00:21:16,510 --> 00:21:19,700
I believe in you because I love you!

289
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:23,180
Just loving someone isn't a 
reason to believe in them!

290
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:27,570
If just loving you isn't a 
reason to believe in you...

291
00:21:27,570 --> 00:21:31,320
Then who the hell would willingly 
go through all this suffering

292
00:21:31,320 --> 00:21:34,980
to come and help a pain 
in the ass like you?!

293
00:21:34,980 --> 00:21:38,290
I love you so much it makes me crazy!

294
00:21:38,290 --> 00:21:40,360
I love you so much I could die!

295
00:21:40,590 --> 00:21:43,320
That's why I put up with 
the pain and suffering!

296
00:21:43,320 --> 00:21:46,620
Even now, I feel like I might puke, 
but I'm still standing in front of you!

297
00:21:47,520 --> 00:21:50,630
I never asked you to do that!

298
00:21:50,630 --> 00:21:52,320
You're just being selfish!

299
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:56,370
You're not thinking about my feelings at all!

300
00:21:56,370 --> 00:21:59,250
You have no idea how 
I feel every time I see you

301
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:02,590
getting hurt because of me!

302
00:22:02,590 --> 00:22:05,730
How <i>would</i> I know?! I don't 
even think about it!

303
00:22:05,730 --> 00:22:09,680
All I think about is how to 
look good in front of you!

304
00:22:09,680 --> 00:22:11,810
I'm suffering for you here!

305
00:22:11,810 --> 00:22:14,080
At least try to look as 
cute as I hoped you would!

306
00:22:14,080 --> 00:22:16,140
Don't talk like I'm just some doll!

307
00:22:16,140 --> 00:22:18,770
Why did you break your promise?!

308
00:22:18,770 --> 00:22:21,520
If you'd just done what I asked you to,
 that would've been enough!

309
00:22:21,520 --> 00:22:23,480
Why wouldn't you even do that?!

310
00:22:23,480 --> 00:22:25,810
You actually hate me, don't you?!

311
00:22:25,810 --> 00:22:26,460
I love you!

312
00:22:26,460 --> 00:22:27,070
Liar!

313
00:22:27,070 --> 00:22:28,910
I'm not lying! I love you!

314
00:22:28,910 --> 00:22:30,030
Then...

315
00:22:33,420 --> 00:22:34,480
Why?

316
00:22:35,230 --> 00:22:37,630
Why did you break your promise?

317
00:22:39,340 --> 00:22:40,470
I can't tell you.

318
00:22:40,870 --> 00:22:44,170
If you'd stayed with me until 
morning like you promised,

319
00:22:44,650 --> 00:22:47,720
I think I could have believed you.

320
00:22:47,720 --> 00:22:51,180
I could have believed you and 
entrusted you with everything.

321
00:22:52,370 --> 00:22:54,800
But you...

322
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:07,300
Since Puck left, my memories 
have been slowly coming back.

323
00:23:07,780 --> 00:23:10,500
Sights in my mind that I don't recognize...

324
00:23:10,500 --> 00:23:12,280
Conversations I don't remember...

325
00:23:12,940 --> 00:23:14,660
More and more of them keep coming back.

326
00:23:15,220 --> 00:23:18,790
I thought I remembered 
everything all this time,

327
00:23:19,730 --> 00:23:23,410
but I went and forgot them, 
as if they never existed.

328
00:23:25,860 --> 00:23:27,800
When all the memories come back,

329
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:30,470
what's going to happen to me?

330
00:23:31,190 --> 00:23:33,710
Is this me... really me?

331
00:23:34,180 --> 00:23:36,310
I forgot so many important things.

332
00:23:36,560 --> 00:23:38,890
I even forgot about Mother.

333
00:23:39,760 --> 00:23:43,710
And yet... I'm not wrong?

334
00:23:47,760 --> 00:23:51,150
<i>What matters isn't how you start 
or what happens in the middle.</i>

335
00:23:51,750 --> 00:23:53,360
<i>It's how it ends.</i>

336
00:23:55,100 --> 00:23:58,160
<i>Yeah... you're right, Mom.</i>

337
00:24:00,790 --> 00:24:03,690
No matter what memories you get back,

338
00:24:03,690 --> 00:24:05,240
it won't change anything.

339
00:24:06,550 --> 00:24:08,250
I love you.

340
00:24:08,690 --> 00:24:10,260
I'm always going to love you.

341
00:24:11,870 --> 00:24:13,850
I can't believe that.

342
00:24:14,350 --> 00:24:22,010
If the me that you say you love... 
g-goes away, could you still...

343
00:24:22,010 --> 00:24:23,170
I could.

344
00:24:23,170 --> 00:24:26,850
No matter what happens, 
you're not going to go away.

345
00:24:27,340 --> 00:24:28,980
I love you.

346
00:24:29,310 --> 00:24:30,860
But you're a liar!

347
00:24:31,680 --> 00:24:34,410
You wouldn't make me believe you.

348
00:24:35,190 --> 00:24:37,280
Then I'll make you believe me now.

349
00:24:40,290 --> 00:24:41,190
Suba—

350
00:24:41,590 --> 00:24:43,000
If you don't want this, then dodge.

351
00:25:14,900 --> 00:25:16,160
I love you.

352
00:25:16,720 --> 00:25:18,690
No matter how many hopeless 
sides of you I see,

353
00:25:18,690 --> 00:25:20,690
and even if we argue like this...

354
00:25:20,690 --> 00:25:23,840
I'm never going to stop loving you.

355
00:25:24,370 --> 00:25:26,560
That won't change, no matter what happens.

356
00:25:27,210 --> 00:25:29,130
I'll just love you even more than before.

357
00:25:29,550 --> 00:25:32,800
That's why I'll always believe in you.

358
00:25:33,570 --> 00:25:35,090
And if you want to know why...

359
00:25:36,820 --> 00:25:38,650
Because... you love me?

360
00:25:42,750 --> 00:25:45,250
With all those unfamiliar 
memories flooding you,

361
00:25:45,250 --> 00:25:47,690
it's only natural that you'd 
feel anxious and scared.

362
00:25:48,340 --> 00:25:50,900
But the path you've walked 
until now won't go away.

363
00:25:52,080 --> 00:25:54,030
You're going to be fine.

364
00:25:54,340 --> 00:25:58,080
How can you say that for sure?

365
00:25:58,730 --> 00:26:00,830
What matters isn't how you start.

366
00:26:00,830 --> 00:26:02,160
It's how it ends.

367
00:26:03,910 --> 00:26:07,370
The woman I respect the most 
in the whole world said so.

368
00:26:08,050 --> 00:26:09,950
You'll be fine, Emilia.

369
00:26:10,740 --> 00:26:12,770
I'm on your side.

370
00:26:12,770 --> 00:26:14,530
It's okay if you remember everything.

371
00:26:15,340 --> 00:26:18,300
And if you're still scared, we'll find it.

372
00:26:18,570 --> 00:26:20,860
Find... what?

373
00:26:22,320 --> 00:26:26,190
Just like my feelings for you make 
me able to keep running forward,

374
00:26:26,660 --> 00:26:30,840
you'll find your most precious feeling, 
the one that makes you able to blow away

375
00:26:30,840 --> 00:26:32,520
all the anxieties and run forward.

376
00:26:34,730 --> 00:26:39,900
Of course, I'd like to hope that 
precious feeling will be for me.

377
00:26:41,180 --> 00:26:44,100
My most... precious feeling...

378
00:26:46,690 --> 00:26:51,680
I wonder if it's among all these 
memories I've been getting back.

379
00:26:52,170 --> 00:26:54,170
My most precious feeling...

380
00:26:55,280 --> 00:26:57,070
Yeah, I'm sure it is.

381
00:26:57,610 --> 00:26:59,340
Your reason to keep walking is there.

382
00:27:08,690 --> 00:27:09,350
Yeah.

383
00:27:09,810 --> 00:27:14,820
A Reason to Believe

384
00:27:24,470 --> 00:27:26,290
Hey. Sorry to keep you waiting.

385
00:27:26,580 --> 00:27:29,200
Ain't like I was waitin' for you.

386
00:27:29,200 --> 00:27:39,200


